Z||000000||Kage86GT4SP||12-06-1999||04:48 AM||||My passenger side headlight goes up alright, but when I turn the lights to the "off" position, the light goes down, but the motor keeps turning, even after the light is all the way down.<P>When I disconnect the single wire that bypasses the relay, the motor stops.  The light will go up with that wire disconnected, but will not go down.  I manually hook up the wire to get the light to drop to the down position, then disconnect it.<P>Is this a relay or a motor problem... and, any ideas to solve short of component replacement?<P>Thanx<P>86 SE 2.8 4 - (STB Turbo 5)MSD5/Blaster<BR>86 Trans Am - stroked '89 vette 350 (383)/ported-TPI/heads port&polish/700R4/Vette OEM stall (2400)/MSD6A/Blaster/SLP Stainless headers/3 inch cat/Edelbrock catback/ and a chip to be announced later.||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||12-06-1999||07:26 AM||||Sounds like if could be the nylon gears stripped out, at least this is a faily common problem. Took the motor housing apart, sometimes they're riveted and you have to drill the rivets out and put it back together with small bolts and or screws. Clean all the old gunky grease out, rotate the nylon gear 180 degrees (only part of it is actually used), then regrease it.||||reg||1
